# VOID -- deep space, and the quietest thing in the book.
#
# Originally written for VECTRENCH and imported from that project's score book:
# https://github.com/cfreder2/VECTRENCH  (src/songs.js)
#
# The opposite of SCRAMBLE in every respect, which is why both are here. 96 BPM
# against 150. No arpeggio at all -- the channel that usually supplies harmony is
# simply not used, and the harmony comes instead from held DYADS in the second
# voice, most of them a tritone. Nothing walks: the bass is a pedal that shudders
# a half-step and returns.
#
# It is the track to reach for when asking whether an arrangement needs density.
# Three sections and eight slots carry two minutes, and it does not feel short of
# material -- because the space IS the material.

@track void
  name   VOID
  bpm    96
  beats  16
  era    8bit
  tags   vectrench game original

@section A
@voice lead inst=lead mix=0.21 tilt=3
